Package: scicomm
Title: Assess Fidelity and Audience Fit in Science Communication
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Assesses how a scientific result is communicated to different
    audiences, such as specialists, students and the general public. A
    result is described once, in a structured way (direction, effect,
    certainty, study design, population and limitations), and each text that
    communicates it is checked against it: whether its language is causal
    when the design is not, whether findings from animals are presented as
    if they applied to people, whether numbers and limitations are kept,
    and whether certainty is overstated. It also reports clarity and
    accessibility indicators for English and Spanish, including the Flesch
    reading ease and the Szigriszt-Pazos perspicuity index, compares the
    versions written for each audience, and writes a self-contained HTML
    report. Indicators are transparent proxies, reported one by one without
    a composite score; whether readers understand a message can only be
    shown by studies with readers.
